WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.192 --> 00:00:04.134
Their composition is also of great
interest to laboratories.

00:00:05.034 --> 00:00:08.175
They search for something unexpected in a
rocky world.

00:00:08.636 --> 00:00:11.757
Organic compounds such as amino acids.

00:00:12.597 --> 00:00:17.900
If you look at the outside of meteorites,
you can see that as they enter the Earth's

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.900
atmosphere,

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:20.841
they can experience some heating and
melting,

00:00:21.261 --> 00:00:28.004
but the interior components of the
meteorite that were shielded from the

00:00:28.004 --> 00:00:30.004
heating upon entering Earth's atmosphere.

00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:31.758
Those are what we're interested in when
we're looking for amino acids.

00:00:33.379 --> 00:00:40.282
Every form of life on Earth contains amino
acids, so asteroids are scientific

00:00:40.282 --> 00:00:42.282
treasure troves.

00:00:42.944 --> 00:00:46.626
Amino acids are the basic subunit that
make up proteins,

00:00:47.406 --> 00:00:51.168
and when we study meteorites and we look
for organic compounds like amino acids,

00:00:51.688 --> 00:00:58.032
it gives us clues as to what types of
chemical compounds meteorites may have

00:00:58.032 --> 00:01:00.032
deposited onto the surface of the Earth.

00:01:00.032 --> 00:01:00.509
at or near the time of the origin of life.

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:07.292
Meteorites and asteroids are ambassadors
from a bygone world.

00:01:09.553 --> 00:01:13.874
Meteorites are particularly interesting
because they contain a chemical record of

00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:15.874
the solar system.

00:01:20.357 --> 00:01:27.020
So laboratories collect meteorites to
understand the composition of asteroids or

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.020
to try and prove that life on

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.226
Earth ...is extraterrestrial in origin.

00:01:44.618 --> 00:01:51.104
There are many building blocks of life
that have been found in meteorites to

00:01:51.104 --> 00:01:53.104
date, but there are still some that have
not yet been found.

00:01:53.104 --> 00:01:58.696
And some of our future research and the
future research in the field will be

00:01:58.696 --> 00:02:00.696
focused on finding those missing links

00:02:00.696 --> 00:02:02.696
in the building blocks of life.

00:02:03.578 --> 00:02:07.640
But scientists have realized that while
meteorites provide clues,

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.843
they are not enough to confirm where life
on Earth originated.

